messages:
elaine: Quick sync — going to batch up docs redirects + snippet updates for v1->v2 model swap. I opened a 'redirect playbook' PR and want quick eyes on telemetry and examples. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/2489
michael: thanks. can we include a small note about token billing change when switching model variants? That confused a user last week.
elaine: yes — planning a callout. also need a minimal code example for client redirect:
```js
// fallback client example
if (resp.status === 404) {
  // switch to v2 client
  client = new RedwoodV2({ key: process.env.RW_KEY });
}
```
samir: small nit: don't advise programmatic 404 switch unless idempotent. prefer checking error code: `error.code === 'MODEL_DEPRECATED'` or use `X-Model-Variant` header.
elaine: good point. I'll add server-side redirect snippet and a client-side soft-fallback block. server snippet:
```nginx
location /api/v1/ {
  return 301 /api/v2/;
}
```
anya: for PR queue — assigning reviewers: @michael, @samir, @jack. @dev-bot can you add labels `migration`,`redirects`,`docs-pr`?
dev-bot: label applied: migration, redirects, docs-pr — PR #2489
jack: I'll take the examples section. Can we also add a brief note about model aliasing + fallback policy? One-liner + link to runtime docs.
elaine: yes, will add aliasing snippet + link to runtime page: https://redwood.ai/docs/runtime/fallbacks
michael: also add a short migration checklist: update client, test embeddings, verify latency on Dedicated. Keep it short.
samir: sample tests to include: smoke gen, embedding stability, and regen evals for top-5 prompts.
elaine: action items: elaine — update PR w/ client snippet + aliasing; jack — examples; michael — check billing wording; samir — review fallback wording. aiming to merge by EOD tomorrow. :calendar:
anya: noted. I'll queue a docs release note for next release train.
